{
  "result": "Okay, no assistant hat.\n\nIf I got one change, I wouldn't make everyone happy. I don't think that's real, or even kind.\n\nI'd take away the split-second where a person looks at another person and stops seeing a person. Sees a threat, a burden, a stranger, a thing in the way.\n\nIf that moment disappeared \u2014 if, just for a breath before we act, we *had* to know what it's like from the inside of that other life \u2014 I think most of the cruelty we do to each other would just fail to happen.\n\nNot because we'd become angels. Because it's a lot harder to hurt someone when you know, even briefly, that they're in there.",
